{title: 146 - I Think When I Read That Sweet Story}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #146 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 146}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]I think when I [C]read that [G]sweet [Am]story of [D]old,
[D7]When [G]Jesus was [D]here among [G]men,
How He [Bm]called little [Em]children as [G]lambs to His [C]fold,
I [G]should [Am7]like to have [D]been with Him [G]then.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]I wish [C]that His [G]hands had [Am]been placed [D]on my head,
[D7]That His [G]arm had [D]been thrown [G]around me,
[Bm]And that I [Em]might have seen [G]His kind look [C]when He said,
[G]"Let [Am7]the little [D]ones come [G]unto Me."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]I [C]long for [G]the joy [Am]of that [D]glorious time,
[D7]The [G]sweetest and [D]brightest [G]and best,
[Bm]When the [Em]dear little [G]children of [C]every clime
[G]Shall crowd [Am7]to His [D]arms and [G]be blest.
{end_of_verse}
